<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch March cash retail sales rise 2.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch March cash retail sales rise 2.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retail sales rose 2.8 percent in cash terms in March compared with March 1996, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>In volume terms March retail sales were 2.9 percent higher than in March 1996, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>DUTCH RETAIL SALES		  March 97   Feb 97	 March 96</p>
<p>Pct change cash yr/yr		 2.8	 2.1	    0.2</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		104	  91	    102</p>
<p> Pct change prices yr/yr	   -0.1	 0.2	    0.1</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		101	 100	    101</p>
<p> Pct change volume yr/yr	    2.9	 1.8	    0.1</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		103	  91	    100</p>
<p> DUTCH RETAIL SALES IN DETAIL   March 97   Feb 97  Apr 96-Mar 97</p>
<p>						     (pct changes yr/yr)</p>
<p> Food cash				  0.4     -0.7	    3.4</p>
<p> Food prices			     -0.6	0.9	    unch</p>
<p> Food volume				1.0     -1.6	    3.4</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food cash	6.0	4.9	    4.5</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food prices    0.1     -0.2	   -0.1</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food volume    5.8	5.2	    4.7</p>
<p>The Central Bureau of Statistics said on Friday that in March 1997 there was one Friday less for shopping and one Monday more.</p>
<p>Retail sales in the food sector rose only slightly in March, CBS said. The increase in non-food was substantial, it said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
